docs {
  # GET TomTom · Flow Segment Data

  Current traffic speed at a single `point` (lat,lon). This is what fills the
  **Live Network Ribbon** — the server calls it once per corridor segment using
  the on-toll anchors in `lib/jasamarga/tomtom.ts` (ANCHORS), then keeps the
  reading only when `frc` is a motorway/trunk/major road (FRC0/1/2).

  **Style/zoom:** `absolute/10` · **unit:** `KMPH`
  **Used by:** `fetchSegments()` in `lib/jasamarga/tomtom.ts`
  **Free tier:** non-tile request (~2,500/day). The server caches results ~2 min.

  ## Example response (real, KM 0–9 mainline anchor)
  ```json
  {
    "flowSegmentData": {
      "frc": "FRC0",
      "currentSpeed": 74,
      "freeFlowSpeed": 74,
      "currentTravelTime": 325,
      "freeFlowTravelTime": 325,
      "confidence": 1,
      "roadClosure": false,
      "coordinates": { "coordinate": [ { "latitude": -6.2566, "longitude": 106.9090 }, "..." ] }
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Field mapping → `RouteSegment`
  | TomTom | our field |
  |---|---|
  | currentSpeed | `speed` (if `frc` ∈ FRC0/1/2, else baseline) |
  | freeFlowSpeed | used to compute `delay_min` |
  | frc | gate: only trust motorway/trunk/major |
  | roadClosure | forces a near-zero speed |

  `frc` = Functional Road Class: **FRC0** motorway · FRC1 trunk · FRC2 major · FRC3+ smaller roads.
}
